<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.13.3: Comparing Exponential Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01484</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.13.3: Comparing Exponential Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>728abc90-76f2-44d2-990d-479e7646590b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity </title>
      <para>Here are graphs representing two functions and descriptions of two functions.</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Graph of two exponential functions, origin O. time(months) and area (square inches). ">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_06_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <list>
        <item> Function \(f\): The area of a wall that is covered by Mold A, in square inches, doubling every month.</item>
        <item> Function \(g\): The area of a wall that is covered by Mold B, in square inches, tripling every month.</item>
      </list>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Which graph represents each function? Explain your answer.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>Since Mold B is growing more quickly, the graph that shows a greater growth factor (the one starting lower and
    ending higher) is function \(g\) (solid).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>When the mold was first spotted and measured, was there more of Mold A or Mold B? Explain how you know.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>There was more of Mold A. The graph for \(f\) (dashed) shows a greater vertical intercept.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>What does the point \((p,q)\) tell us in this situation? Explain your answer.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>After \(p\) months, there was the same amount of Mold A and Mold B on the wall (\(q\) square inches), after which
    Mold B started to have larger area than Mold A.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
    <note class="self-check">
      (    <para>In the formula \(f(x)=a \cdot b^x\), what changes on the graph when \(a\) changes?</para>)
        </note>
        <section>
          <title>Additional Resources</title>
          
    <section>
      <title>Reading Exponential Graphs</title>
      <para>The graphs of \(f\) and \(g\) are located below and are functions of the form \(y=a \cdot b^x\).</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="GRAPH OF EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTIONS, F AND G. FUNCTION G HAS A SMALLER \(y\)-intercepts AND CLIMBS MORE QUICKLY THAN FUNCTION F.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_08_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <para>Which curve has the larger \(a\) value?</para>
      <para>\(f(x)\) because its \(y\)-intercept is higher.</para>
      <para>Which curve has the larger \(b\) value?</para>
      <para>\(g(x)\) because it is growing more quickly.</para>
      <note class="try look-at-me"/>
  <title>Try It: Reading Exponential Graphs</title>
      <para>The graphs of \(f\) and \(g\) are located below and are functions of the form \(y=ab^x\).</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="GRAPH OF EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTIONS, F AND G. FUNCTION F HAS A SMALLER \(y\)-intercepts AND CLIMBS MORE QUICKLY THAN FUNCTION G.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_08_02.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Which curve has the larger \(b\) value?</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>\(f(x)\) has the larger \(b\) value because it is growing faster than \(g(x)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
        </section>
        
  </content>
